WEBVTT

00:00.459 --> 00:03.578
- [Instructor] We're told
that Mael mixes 15 milliliters

00:03.578 --> 00:06.495
of bleach with 3.75 liters of water

00:07.936 --> 00:10.893
to make a sanitizing
solution for a daycare.

00:10.893 --> 00:12.832
The amounts of bleach and water

00:12.832 --> 00:15.046
always have to be proportional

00:15.046 --> 00:17.810
when he makes the sanitizing solution.

00:17.810 --> 00:20.666
Which of the following could
be combinations of volumes

00:20.666 --> 00:24.607
of bleach and water for
Mael's sanitizing solution?

00:24.607 --> 00:26.598
And they gave us,
actually they gave us five

00:26.598 --> 00:29.463
potential combinations,
they say pick three.

00:29.463 --> 00:30.967
So I encourage you to pause this video

00:30.967 --> 00:32.227
and try to figure it out.

00:32.227 --> 00:34.929
Remember, he mixes 15
milliliters of bleach

00:34.929 --> 00:37.512
for every 3.75 liters of water.

00:40.565 --> 00:43.352
Alright, now let's try
to work this together.

00:43.352 --> 00:44.781
So I'm gonna make a table here.

00:44.781 --> 00:49.761
So let's say this is bleach,
bleach in milliliters.

00:49.761 --> 00:52.844
And lets say this is water in liters.

00:54.657 --> 00:58.490
And they tell us that
he mixes 15 milliliters,

01:00.642 --> 01:01.883
the unit here is milliliters,

01:01.883 --> 01:04.474
for every 15 milliliters of bleach

01:04.474 --> 01:07.057
for every 3.75 liters of water.

01:09.955 --> 01:12.983
So what is the
proportionality constant here?

01:12.983 --> 01:16.529
If you said the water is
equal to some constant

01:16.529 --> 01:19.222
times the bleach, well what's going on?

01:19.222 --> 01:22.482
Well let's see, what would
he have to multiply by?

01:22.482 --> 01:25.982
He would have to multiply by 3.75 over 15.

01:29.381 --> 01:31.964
Now what is 3.75 divided by 15?

01:33.009 --> 01:34.998
Let me actually do it right over here,

01:34.998 --> 01:36.498
15 goes into 3.75.

01:39.044 --> 01:42.053
Let's see, 15 goes into 37 two times,

01:42.053 --> 01:43.261
we have our little
decimal right over here,

01:43.261 --> 01:46.178
two times 15 is 30, subtract seven,

01:48.272 --> 01:52.505
bring down the five and
then 15 times five is 75,

01:52.505 --> 01:55.858
five times 15 is 75, it all works out.

01:55.858 --> 01:58.945
So we see to go from bleach to water

01:58.945 --> 02:03.112
we're multiplying by a
proportionality constant of 0.25.

02:05.855 --> 02:07.328
So we have to see which of these

02:07.328 --> 02:09.807
have the same exact
proportionality constant

02:09.807 --> 02:11.961
going from bleach to water.

02:11.961 --> 02:15.628
So let's see, this next
one is 12 and three.

02:18.064 --> 02:20.481
So if we multiply 12 by 0.25,

02:23.254 --> 02:24.514
do we get three?

02:24.514 --> 02:27.776
Yeah, three is one fourth
of 12, 0.25, 25 hundredths

02:27.776 --> 02:31.655
is the same thing as one
fourth so this one checks out.

02:31.655 --> 02:34.405
What about going from six to 1.5?

02:36.845 --> 02:39.095
Are we multiplying by 0.25?

02:40.211 --> 02:42.711
Yeah, 1.5 is one fourth of six

02:44.077 --> 02:46.103
or another way to think about it is

02:46.103 --> 02:47.853
what is six times 25?

02:49.951 --> 02:52.909
It is a 150 so six times 25 hundredths

02:52.909 --> 02:57.318
would be a 150 hundredths
which is the same thing as 1.5.

02:57.318 --> 02:58.903
So this one works.

02:58.903 --> 03:01.693
What about three and 0.75?

03:01.693 --> 03:03.193
So three and 0.75.

03:05.796 --> 03:07.879
Am I multiplying by 0.25?

03:08.757 --> 03:11.427
Yeah, if I multiply three
times 25 hundredths,

03:11.427 --> 03:14.384
I get 75 hundredths so that works.

03:14.384 --> 03:16.965
So actually the first three
choices are our three answers

03:16.965 --> 03:18.680
but let's just verify that the next two

03:18.680 --> 03:21.069
are not good answers.

03:21.069 --> 03:24.152
So let's see, if I go from 20 to 5.5,

03:27.671 --> 03:30.338
and so am I multiplying by 0.25?

03:31.663 --> 03:34.975
No, 0.25 which is the
same thing as one fourth,

03:34.975 --> 03:38.629
one fourth times 20 is five, not 5.5.

03:38.629 --> 03:39.892
So that doesn't work.

03:39.892 --> 03:42.475
And then going from 11 to 3.75,

03:44.483 --> 03:46.200
well we definitely know
that's not gonna work

03:46.200 --> 03:48.640
because notice we have
the same amount of water

03:48.640 --> 03:50.640
but we have less bleach.

03:51.572 --> 03:53.973
Or you could say what's one fourth of 11?

03:53.973 --> 03:57.327
Well that's going to be less than 3.75

03:57.327 --> 04:00.744
so we can rule both of these choices out.
